MSU-2 Task 2e bare-metal access investigation — 2026-10-16

Before the Linux shutdown, XSCT 2025.1 found Digilent JTAG-SMT2NC serial 210308A46334, the ZCU102 xczu9 TAP, the PS TAP, and four running Cortex-A53 cores.

Linux was gracefully stopped using `sync; poweroff` after all Linux sustained measurements had completed. UART output ended with `reboot: Power down`.

After shutdown, XSCT still identified the TAP chain but reported APU `No Power` and Cortex-A53 `FPD No Power`. The following recovery attempts did not restore an accessible Cortex-A53 target:

- XSCT `rst -system` against the PSU target returned without an error, but target enumeration still showed APU/A53 `No Power`.
- AMD's documented JTAG security-gate unlock (`mwr 0xffca0038 0x1ff`) was attempted. `rdi_xsct` segfaulted and exited before producing a target list; whether the volatile register write completed is unconfirmed.
- The documented `rst -processor` path failed with a closed TCF channel while selecting Cortex-A53 #0.
- The `rst -srst` attempt also ended with a closed TCF channel while selecting the PSU target.
- A subsequent UART check detected no Linux shell prompt and sent no target commands. The saved read-only result is `target_preflight_post_halt.log`.
- A final XSCT probe returned `channel closed` while enumerating targets.

No ELF was downloaded or executed. No FPGA bitstream was reprogrammed, and no SD card, boot image, or persistent board configuration was written. The board's active Linux session is stopped; a physical board power-on/reset is needed before the bare-metal run can continue. No remotely controlled outlet or board power interface is exposed by the workstation session.

AMD references consulted:
- UG1209, Loading U-Boot Using XSCT/XSDB: https://docs.amd.com/r/2024.1-English/ug1209-embedded-design-tutorial/Loading-U-Boot-Using-XSCT/XSDB
- UG1400, Debugging Applications on Zynq UltraScale+ MPSoC: https://docs.amd.com/r/2024.1-English/ug1400-vitis-embedded/Debugging-Applications-on-Zynq-UltraScale-MPSoC
- UG1085, Zynq UltraScale+ Device TRM, System Test and Debug / Power-up Request and Acknowledge: https://docs.amd.com/api/khub/documents/xzMsp_c5sG9J6A3u7NkJYQ/content?Ft-Calling-App=ft
